# The contracts and the typed branches of the filtered structural recursion
# over Scott lists, list_fold_filtered of parallel_lists. Each lemma holds
# for every element type, output type, base and step: list_fold_filtered
# filters the base, the recursive result handed to the step and the step's
# output by the output type, so no lemma here asks anything of the step.
# The lemmas are sound, and they are kept out of the lemma set of HM. They
# are a module of their own so that every lemma set is a union of whole
# modules: a configuration enables them without the lemmas on the
# filtered folds of the naturals.
#
# A typed branch adds to a term a smaller alternative, A = A + B with B ≤ A,
# an equation that holds up to ≃_O, so adding B changes the meaning of no
# term in any context, and dropping A at
# compile time only loses answers.
#
# Every lemma here is a theorem of λ-lattice-unit-η (CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Terms"); each declaration cites its paper proof. None uses
# induction. This module declares no define:
# it uses compose (prelude), nat_type (parallel_types), filter_by,
# list_type, list_fold and list_fold_filtered (parallel_lists), with which
# it is compiled.

